    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6c541a40",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: suddenly_mexico_wants_to_talk_about_immigration; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a formal diplomatic meeting with U.S. Vice President Mike Pence and Mexican officials, but the text overlays suggest a sarcastic or mocking tone implying that Mexico is suddenly interested in immigration discussions only when it is convenient for the U.S. The second text overlay, 'i'm so grateful we have a tough president,' implies that the U.S. president is being portrayed as strong or uncompromising, possibly in a way that is dismissive of Mexico's position. This meme uses juxtaposition to imply that Mexico is only willing to engage in immigration talks under pressure or when it suits the U.S. perspective. The overall intent is to criticize or mock Mexico's stance on immigration, potentially reinforcing negative stereotypes about Mexico being opportunistic or uncooperative. The meme may be harmful as it could contribute to a narrative that portrays Mexico as untrustworthy or unwilling to cooperate on immigration issues, which could fuel anti-immigrant sentiment or xenophobia. The meme does not contain direct abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful language targeting specific individuals or groups, but it does contain harmful content by potentially reinforcing negative stereotypes about Mexico and its government.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bdc60d00"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
